INSERT INTO `route_itineraries` VALUES (1,2,1,'Drive to Besisahar/Dharapani','Long scenic drive from Kathmandu.',1860,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2,2,2,'Trek to Chame','Walk through pine forests and views of Manaslu.',2670,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(3,2,3,'Trek to Pisang','The valley opens up, view of Paungda Danda rock face.',3200,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(4,2,4,'Trek to Manang','Enter the arid high altitude region.',3540,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(5,2,5,'Acclimatization in Manang','Hike to Gangapurna Lake.',3540,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(6,2,9,'Cross Thorong La Pass (5416m)','The biggest day of the trek. Descend to Muktinath.',3760,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(7,3,1,'Drive to Syabrubesi','Winding mountain roads.',1503,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(8,3,2,'Trek to Lama Hotel','Walk through lush rhododendron forests.',2470,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(9,3,3,'Trek to Langtang Village','Rebuilt village after 2015 earthquake.',3430,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(10,3,4,'Trek to Kyanjin Gompa','Final settlement with a cheese factory.',3870,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(11,1,1,'Fly to Lukla, Trek to Phakding','Board an early morning scenic mountain flight from Kathmandu to Lukla (2,840m) — one of the world\'s most thrilling short runways. Meet your trek crew and begin walking through Dudh Koshi valley, passing chortens and mani walls, descending gently to the riverside tea houses of Phakding.',2652,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(12,1,2,'Phakding to Namche Bazaar','Cross several suspension bridges festooned with prayer flags as the trail climbs through pine forest and dramatic gorges. After the final steep 600m climb you reach Namche Bazaar — the vibrant Sherpa capital at 3,440m. First views of Everest and Lhotse on a clear day.',3440,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(13,1,3,'Acclimatization Day in Namche Bazaar','A rest day essential for altitude adaptation. Take an acclimatization hike up to the Everest View Hotel (3,880m) for your first full view of Everest, Lhotse, Ama Dablam, and Thamserku. Browse Namche\'s Saturday market and explore its bakeries, cafes, and trekking shops.',3440,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(14,1,4,'Namche Bazaar to Tengboche','Traverse high above the Dudh Koshi on a breathtaking contour trail with constant Ama Dablam views. Descend to the river and climb through rhododendron forest to the famous Tengboche Monastery — the spiritual heart of the Khumbu — dramatically set against Ama Dablam\'s spire.',3870,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(15,1,5,'Tengboche to Dingboche','Pass through the stone villages of Pangboche and Shomare as the vegetation thins and the high-altitude landscape opens up. Arrive in Dingboche, a wide flat valley surrounded by towering peaks including Lhotse\'s immense south face.',4410,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(16,1,6,'Acclimatization Day in Dingboche','Second critical acclimatization rest day. Hike up to the ridge above Dingboche (approx. 5,100m) for extraordinary views of Makalu, Baruntse, and Island Peak. Return for lunch and an afternoon rest before tomorrow\'s higher terrain.',4410,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(17,1,7,'Dingboche to Lobuche','Trek across the moraine of the Khumbu Glacier past the poignant memorial chortens for mountaineers who lost their lives on Everest. The landscape becomes stark and lunar as you arrive at Lobuche — a collection of tea houses in a narrow valley beneath Lobuche Peak.',4910,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(18,1,8,'Lobuche to Gorak Shep and Everest Base Camp','Walk across the rough lateral moraine of the Khumbu Glacier to the highest tea houses in the world at Gorak Shep (5,164m). After lunch make the iconic 2-hour walk across glacial rubble to Everest Base Camp (5,364m) — stand at the foot of the world\'s highest mountain. Return to Gorak Shep.',5164,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(19,1,9,'Kala Patthar Sunrise, Trek to Pheriche','Rise at 4am to climb Kala Patthar (5,545m) before dawn. Watch the sun turn Everest\'s summit pyramid gold as it rises above the horizon — the quintessential Himalayan moment. Descend all the way to Pheriche for a well-earned rest and hearty meal.',4371,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(20,1,10,'Pheriche to Namche Bazaar','A long but rewarding descent through familiar terrain, dropping over 900 vertical metres. The body feels stronger at lower altitude. Stop at Tengboche for lunch and enjoy the downhill trail through rhododendron forest back to Namche.',3440,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(21,1,11,'Namche Bazaar to Lukla','The final trekking day follows the river downhill through Phakding back to the busy mountain airstrip town of Lukla. Celebrate over dinner with your guide and porter crew.',2840,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(22,1,12,'Fly Lukla to Kathmandu','Morning flight back to Kathmandu (weather permitting). Arrive to the warmth of the city, hot shower, and the welcome comfort of a real bed. Transfer to your hotel.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(23,1,13,'Kathmandu — Rest and Sightseeing','Free day to explore Kathmandu: visit Thamel, Boudhanath Stupa, or the Pashupatinath temple complex. Optional Yeti Routes-arranged cultural tours available. Farewell dinner with your guide.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(24,1,14,'Departure','Transfer to Tribhuvan International Airport for your onward flight. Your Everest adventure ends here — with memories that will last a lifetime.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(25,2,6,'Manang to Yak Kharka','Leave the last significant settlement behind and trek through high-altitude scrub into the barren upper valley. The trail follows the Marsyangdi river upstream past grazing yaks to the simple tea houses of Yak Kharka. Views of Chulu East and West peaks are excellent.',4018,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(26,2,7,'Yak Kharka to Thorong High Camp','A short but important acclimatization walk to the tea houses just below the Thorong La approach. Arrive early, rest thoroughly, and eat well. Tomorrow is the biggest day of the circuit — prepare gear, headlamps, and warm layers the evening before.',4925,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(27,2,8,'Rest/Buffer Day at Thorong High Camp','Optional rest day to acclimatize fully before the pass crossing. Use the time to hydrate, eat carbohydrate-rich food, and take a short acclimatization stroll above camp. Check weather forecast for pass conditions.',4925,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(28,2,10,'Muktinath to Marpha via Jomsom','Descend the dramatic Mustang plateau landscape to the holy town of Jomsom and continue to the apple orchards of Marpha. The katabatic winds of the Kali Gandaki typically kick in by midday — aim to be off the trail early. Enjoy Marpha\'s famous apple brandy and cider in the evening.',2665,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(29,2,11,'Marpha to Kalopani','Follow the Kali Gandaki river — the world\'s deepest gorge — through Tibetan-influenced villages. Dhaulagiri (8,167m) and Annapurna I (8,091m) loom above on either side, making this one of the most dramatic single-day stages of any trek in Nepal.',2530,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(30,2,12,'Kalopani to Tatopani','Descend through subtropical forests back to the warmth of lower valleys. Tatopani means \"hot water\" — reward yourself with a long soak in the famous natural hot springs on the banks of the Kali Gandaki after days of high-altitude trekking.',1190,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(31,2,13,'Tatopani to Ghorepani','A steep 1,700m climb through dense rhododendron forest — demanding but beautiful, especially in spring. Arrive at Ghorepani with energy for sunset views from the ridge above if the clouds cooperate.',2874,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(32,2,14,'Poon Hill Sunrise, Trek to Nayapul','Rise at dawn for the short climb to Poon Hill (3,210m) — one of Nepal\'s most celebrated sunrise viewpoints. Watch the full Annapurna and Dhaulagiri ranges light up at first light. Descend through Ghandruk to Nayapul and drive to Pokhara.',820,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(33,2,15,'Pokhara to Kathmandu','Drive or fly from Pokhara to Kathmandu. The scenic Prithvi Highway follows the river valleys and offers mountain glimpses on clear days. Afternoon at leisure in Kathmandu.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(34,2,16,'Departure','Transfer to Tribhuvan International Airport for your onward journey. The Annapurna Circuit — one of the world\'s great walks — is complete.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(35,3,5,'Acclimatization Day at Kyanjin Gompa','Rest and acclimatize at Kyanjin Gompa. Hike up Kyanjin Ri (4,773m) for a stunning 360° panorama of Langtang Lirung (7,227m), Langtang II, Dorje Lakpa, and the broad Langtang Glacier. The yak cheese dairy here is worth a visit. Return to Kyanjin for the night.',3870,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(36,3,6,'Kyanjin Gompa to Lama Hotel','Begin the return journey, descending back through Langtang Village and the beautiful rhododendron and bamboo forests. The trail feels easier on the way down and the lower altitude brings renewed energy. Lama Hotel sits beside a tumbling mountain stream.',2470,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(37,3,7,'Lama Hotel to Syabrubesi','Complete the valley descent back to the road-head at Syabrubesi. Cross the roaring Langtang Khola and pass through scattered villages as the forest thickens and the air warms. Afternoon free in Syabrubesi.',1503,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(38,3,8,'Drive Syabrubesi to Kathmandu','Bumpy but scenic 7–8 hour drive back to Kathmandu through forested hills, river valleys, and mountain towns. Arrive in Kathmandu by late afternoon. Hotel check-in and rest.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(39,3,9,'Kathmandu — Rest and Sightseeing','Free day in Kathmandu. Optional visits to Boudhanath Stupa, Pashupatinath Temple, or Thamel. Yeti Routes farewell dinner with your guide in the evening.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(40,3,10,'Departure','Transfer to Tribhuvan International Airport for your onward flight. Langtang Valley — the valley of glaciers — will stay with you long after you leave.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(41,4,1,'Drive Kathmandu to Soti Khola','Early morning drive along the Prithvi Highway and then up the Budhi Gandaki river valley to the dusty road-head at Soti Khola. The drive takes around 7 hours through increasingly dramatic gorge scenery.',700,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(42,4,2,'Soti Khola to Machha Khola','First full day of trekking along the Budhi Gandaki river on a trail through rice paddies, subtropical forest, and small farming villages. Cross several suspension bridges as the valley narrows.',869,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(43,4,3,'Machha Khola to Jagat','The trail climbs steadily through more remote terrain past waterfalls and cliff-face trails. Jagat is the checkpoint where Manaslu Restricted Area permits are verified. Enjoy the first distant views of the Himalayan peaks ahead.',1410,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(44,4,4,'Jagat to Deng','Pass through Philim village — an important cultural gateway — and enter progressively wilder landscape. The valley narrows and the trail crosses and re-crosses the river. Deng sits at a widening of the valley with good mountain views.',1804,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(45,4,5,'Deng to Namrung','Trek through the gorge past the dramatic side valley leading toward Tibet. The culture shifts noticeably — mani walls, gompas, and prayer flags indicate the increasing Tibetan Buddhist influence. First views of Manaslu\'s upper slopes begin to appear.',2630,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(46,4,6,'Namrung to Samagaon via Lho','Pass through Lho village for spectacular close-up views of Manaslu\'s north face — one of the most dramatic mountain faces in the Himalayas. Descend slightly to Samagaon, a large Tibetan-origin village with an ancient gompa.',3530,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(47,4,7,'Acclimatization Day in Samagaon','Essential acclimatization rest day. Optional day hike toward Manaslu Base Camp (4,480m) for outstanding close-up views of the 8,163m summit. Explore Samagaon\'s gompa and interact with local Nubri people.',3530,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(48,4,8,'Samagaon to Samdo','Short but important ascent to the last permanent settlement before the high pass. Samdo sits in an open valley close to the Tibetan border. Cold nights here prepare the body for the pass crossing.',3875,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(49,4,9,'Samdo to Dharamsala (Larkya Phedi)','Climb to the base camp for the Larkya La crossing. Dharamsala means \"resting place\" — it\'s a small collection of tea houses at the foot of the pass. Arrive early in the afternoon, rest well, eat a big dinner, and prepare for a very early start.',4460,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(50,4,10,'Cross Larkya La Pass (5,160m) to Bimthang','Start well before dawn (3–4am) to cross the Larkya La in good conditions. The ascent is steep and the pass high, but the views of Manaslu, Himlung, Cheo, Annapurna II and Lamjung Himal on the descent are staggering. A long, glorious day ending at flower-filled Bimthang.',3590,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(51,4,11,'Bimthang to Tilje','Descend rapidly from the high-altitude world through rhododendron forest and past yak pastures. The Dudh Khola river valley opens up and warmth returns. Tilje is a small but welcoming settlement.',2300,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(52,4,12,'Tilje to Dharapani','Complete the descent to the main Annapurna Circuit trailhead at Dharapani, joining the paved road. The Manaslu Circuit is complete. Drive begins back toward Besisahar and Kathmandu.',1960,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(53,4,13,'Drive to Kathmandu','Full-day drive through the Marsyangdi river valley and back along the Prithvi Highway to Kathmandu. Arrive in the evening. Hotel check-in, hot shower, and well-deserved rest.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(54,4,14,'Departure','Transfer to Tribhuvan International Airport. The Manaslu Circuit — one of Nepal\'s most rewarding and least-commercialised treks — is complete.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(55,20,1,'Fly to Lukla, Trek to Phakding','Board an early morning scenic mountain flight from Kathmandu to Lukla (2,840m). Meet your trek crew and begin walking through Dudh Koshi valley past chortens and mani walls to the riverside tea houses of Phakding.',2652,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(56,20,2,'Phakding to Namche Bazaar','Cross suspension bridges through pine forest and dramatic gorges. After the final steep 600m climb you reach Namche Bazaar — the Sherpa capital. First views of Everest on a clear day.',3440,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(57,20,3,'Acclimatization Day in Namche Bazaar','Acclimatization hike to Everest View Hotel (3,880m) for a full view of Everest, Lhotse, and Ama Dablam. Browse Namche\'s famous Saturday market and explore the town.',3440,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(58,20,4,'Namche Bazaar to Tengboche','High contour trail with constant Ama Dablam views, descend to the river and climb through rhododendron forest to Tengboche Monastery — the spiritual heart of the Khumbu.',3870,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(59,20,5,'Tengboche to Dingboche','Pass through Pangboche and Shomare as vegetation thins. Arrive in the wide flat Dingboche valley beneath Lhotse\'s immense south face.',4410,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(60,20,6,'Acclimatization Day in Dingboche','Hike up to the ridge above Dingboche (~5,100m) for views of Makalu, Baruntse, and Island Peak. Essential for altitude adaptation before the higher terrain ahead.',4410,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(61,20,7,'Dingboche to Lobuche','Trek across the moraine past the mountaineers\' memorial chortens. The landscape becomes stark and lunar as you reach Lobuche beneath its namesake peak.',4910,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(62,20,8,'Lobuche to Gorak Shep and Everest Base Camp','Walk across glacial moraine to Gorak Shep (5,164m), then the iconic walk to Everest Base Camp (5,364m). Stand at the foot of the world\'s highest mountain. Return to Gorak Shep.',5164,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(63,20,9,'Kala Patthar Sunrise, Trek to Pheriche','Pre-dawn climb to Kala Patthar (5,545m) for the most famous Everest sunrise photograph on earth. Descend all the way to Pheriche for rest.',4371,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(64,20,10,'Pheriche to Namche Bazaar','Long descent through familiar terrain, dropping 900m. Stop at Tengboche for lunch and continue through rhododendron forest back to Namche.',3440,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(65,20,11,'Namche Bazaar to Lukla','Final trekking day follows the river downhill to Lukla. Celebrate over dinner with your guide and porter crew.',2840,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(66,20,12,'Fly Lukla to Kathmandu','Morning flight back to Kathmandu. Transfer to hotel.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(67,20,13,'Kathmandu — Rest and Sightseeing','Free day in Kathmandu. Optional cultural tours. Farewell dinner with your guide.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(68,20,14,'Departure','Transfer to Tribhuvan International Airport. Your Everest adventure is complete.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(69,22,1,'Fly to Lukla, Trek to Phakding','Morning mountain flight Kathmandu–Lukla (2,840m). Begin the trek down through the Dudh Koshi gorge to Phakding, passing the first mani walls and prayer flags of the Khumbu.',2652,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(70,22,2,'Phakding to Namche Bazaar','Cross suspension bridges over the roaring Dudh Koshi and climb steeply to Namche Bazaar, the gateway to the Everest region. First glimpse of Everest on a clear day.',3440,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(71,22,3,'Acclimatization in Namche Bazaar','Essential rest day. Hike to Everest View Hotel (3,880m) for panoramic views of Everest, Lhotse, and Ama Dablam. Explore Namche\'s monastery, museum, and lively market.',3440,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(72,22,4,'Namche to Dole via Mong La','Leave the main EBC trail and take the quieter Gokyo route, climbing through juniper and rhododendron forest via Mong La viewpoint. Dole sits in open terrain above the treeline.',4038,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(73,22,5,'Dole to Machherma','Continue up the broad valley through yak pastures and stone herders\' huts. Machherma is a small settlement famous in local lore for a legendary yeti encounter. Views of Cho Oyu appear.',4410,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(74,22,6,'Machherma to Gokyo','Reach the shores of the first Gokyo Lake and continue to the iconic blue-green waters of the third lake (Dudh Pokhari) at Gokyo village. The Ngozumpa Glacier — Nepal\'s largest — fills the horizon.',4790,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(75,22,7,'Gokyo Ri Summit and Lake Exploration','Pre-dawn climb to Gokyo Ri (5,357m) for one of Nepal\'s finest mountain panoramas — four 8,000m giants visible including Everest, Lhotse, Makalu, and Cho Oyu. Afternoon: explore the 4th and 5th Gokyo Lakes if energy permits.',4790,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(76,22,8,'Gokyo to Namche Bazaar','Begin the return journey, descending back along the western Gokyo valley. Long but mostly downhill day returning to the warmth and comfort of Namche Bazaar.',3440,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(77,22,9,'Namche Bazaar to Lukla','Final day of trekking follows the river trail back down through Phakding to Lukla. Farewell dinner with your crew.',2840,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(78,22,10,'Fly Lukla to Kathmandu','Morning flight back to Kathmandu. Hotel check-in, hot shower, and rest.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(79,22,11,'Kathmandu Sightseeing','Free day: Boudhanath Stupa, Pashupatinath, or Thamel shopping. Optional Yeti Routes-arranged city tour.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(80,22,12,'Departure','Transfer to Tribhuvan International Airport for your onward journey.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(81,23,1,'Fly to Lukla, Trek to Phakding','Mountain flight Kathmandu–Lukla. First steps on the trail through the Dudh Koshi gorge to Phakding.',2652,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(82,23,2,'Phakding to Namche Bazaar','Dramatic trail through forests and gorges to Namche Bazaar, the Everest region\'s hub.',3440,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(83,23,3,'Acclimatization Day in Namche Bazaar','Rest day with acclimatization hike to Everest View Hotel. Explore Namche\'s vibrant market.',3440,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(84,23,4,'Namche Bazaar to Tengboche','High-contour trail with extraordinary Ama Dablam views. Arrive at Tengboche Monastery in the late afternoon.',3870,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(85,23,5,'Tengboche to Dingboche','Trek past Pangboche through the upper Imja Khola valley to Dingboche, surrounded by 7,000m peaks.',4410,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(86,23,6,'Acclimatization Day in Dingboche','Altitude adaptation day. Hike the ridge above Dingboche for views of Makalu and Island Peak. Rest in the afternoon.',4410,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(87,23,7,'Dingboche to Ama Dablam Base Camp','Leave the main EBC trail and take the trail toward the south-west face of Ama Dablam. The base camp sits in a dramatic cirque directly below the hanging glacier that makes Ama Dablam so distinctive. Spectacular close-up photography.',4570,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(88,23,8,'Explore Ama Dablam BC, Return to Dingboche','Morning exploration around the base camp area with views of climbing routes on the mountain\'s ridges. Return to Dingboche for the night, enjoying the altitude gain benefits.',4410,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(89,23,9,'Dingboche to Namche Bazaar','Long but downhill return day via Tengboche. The descent is rapid and energising.',3440,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(90,23,10,'Namche Bazaar to Lukla','Final trekking day down to Lukla. Celebration dinner with crew.',2840,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(91,23,11,'Fly Lukla to Kathmandu','Morning flight back to Kathmandu.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(92,23,12,'Departure','Transfer to Tribhuvan International Airport.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(93,25,1,'Drive Kathmandu to Pokhara','Scenic 6–7 hour drive along the Prithvi Highway following river valleys to Pokhara, Nepal\'s second city and the base for Annapurna treks. Evening stroll along Phewa Lake.',820,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(94,25,2,'Pokhara to Ulleri via Nayapul','Drive to Nayapul and begin trekking through Birethanti into Gurung country. The day ends with the punishing 3,000-step stone staircase up to Ulleri — a genuinely tough introduction to the trek.',2073,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(95,25,3,'Ulleri to Ghorepani','Continue climbing through dense rhododendron forest (spectacular in bloom March–April) to Ghorepani — a ridge-top village with sweeping Himalayan views and the start of the famous Poon Hill trail.',2874,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(96,25,4,'Poon Hill Sunrise, Trek to Chhomrong','Pre-dawn climb to Poon Hill (3,210m) for sunrise over Dhaulagiri and Annapurna. Descend via Tadapani through diverse forest zones to the large Gurung village of Chhomrong — the last major settlement before the Annapurna Sanctuary.',2170,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(97,25,5,'Chhomrong to Dovan via Sinuwa','Enter the gorge leading into the Annapurna Sanctuary. The trail descends steeply into the Modi Khola gorge then climbs back up through dense forest. The walls close in as you enter the famous Annapurna \"bamboo zone.\"',2600,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(98,25,6,'Dovan to Machhapuchhre Base Camp','Trek out of the dense forest into open alpine terrain. The sacred Machhapuchhre (6,993m) — whose summit has never been climbed — towers directly above. MBC offers the first unobstructed views into the sanctuary.',3700,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(99,25,7,'MBC to Annapurna Base Camp','The final approach to the sanctuary. Walk across glacial moraines and boulder fields into the extraordinary 360° amphitheatre of Annapurna Base Camp (4,130m), encircled by Annapurna I, II, III, IV, South, Machhapuchhre, Gangapurna, and Hiunchuli. A genuinely humbling experience.',4130,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(100,25,8,'ABC to Bamboo','Begin the descent, taking in the sanctuary views for the last time. Descend rapidly through MBC and back into the forest zone, reaching Bamboo by early afternoon.',2310,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(101,25,9,'Bamboo to Jhinu Danda Hot Spring, Drive to Pokhara','Descend to Jhinu Danda and soak in the famous natural hot springs on the Modi Khola riverbank — a perfect celebration of completing the trek. Drive or trek to Nayapul and transfer to Pokhara.',820,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(102,25,10,'Drive Pokhara to Kathmandu or Departure','Drive back to Kathmandu or take the morning flight. Tour ends on arrival.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(103,27,1,'Drive Kathmandu to Chamje','Drive along the Prithvi Highway and up the Marsyangdi valley to Chamje, the starting point for this northern Annapurna approach.',1430,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(104,27,2,'Chamje to Dharapani','Trek upriver through waterfalls and gorge scenery to Dharapani, where the Manaslu and Annapurna Circuit trails diverge.',1960,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(105,27,3,'Dharapani to Chame','Enter the Annapurna Conservation Area. The trail follows the Marsyangdi river through pine and cedar forest with first high-peak views. Chame is the administrative hub of Manang district.',2670,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(106,27,4,'Chame to Manang','One of the great stages of any Himalayan trek — pass the enormous rock face of Paungda Danda, cross the dramatic Upper Pisang ridge, and arrive in Manang with views of the entire Annapurna range.',3540,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(107,27,5,'Acclimatization Day in Manang','Essential rest day before heading higher. Hike to Gangapurna Lake (3,540m) or the Ice Lake (4,600m) for views of Annapurna III and Gangapurna glacier. Attend the daily altitude sickness lecture at the Himalayan Rescue Association clinic.',3540,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(108,27,6,'Manang to Khangsar','Take the high trail north from Manang toward the Tibetan plateau, entering the northern Annapurna approach valley. Khangsar is the last village before the high ground.',3734,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(109,27,7,'Khangsar to North Annapurna Base Camp Viewpoint','Ascend to the spectacular viewpoint area on the north side of the Annapurna massif (approx. 4,500m) with extraordinary views of the northern faces of Annapurna II, III, and IV, plus the Tilicho plateau. Return to Khangsar.',3734,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(110,27,8,'Khangsar to Manang, Drive toward Kathmandu','Return to Manang and begin the drive back down the valley toward Besisahar and Kathmandu.',760,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(111,27,9,'Arrive Kathmandu or Departure','Complete drive to Kathmandu. Tour ends on arrival.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(112,30,1,'Drive Kathmandu to Pokhara','Comfortable drive or flight to Pokhara. Evening lakeside orientation.',820,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(113,30,2,'Drive to Nayapul, Trek to Tikhedhunga','Drive to Nayapul and begin the Annapurna foothills trail through Birethanti. Steady climb to Tikhedhunga.',1540,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(114,30,3,'Tikhedhunga to Ghorepani','Climb the famous stone staircase past Ulleri through stunning rhododendron forest to the ridge-top village of Ghorepani.',2874,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(115,30,4,'Poon Hill Sunrise, Trek to Swanta','Pre-dawn Poon Hill (3,210m) sunrise with Dhaulagiri and Annapurna panorama. Leave the standard trail and descend south to the rarely visited Swanta village, entering Khopra Danda territory.',2200,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(116,30,5,'Swanta to Khopra Danda','Climb steadily through diverse forest and open meadows to the spectacular Khopra Danda ridge (3,660m). The community-run lodge here is one of Nepal\'s most rewarding trekking destinations. Views of Dhaulagiri, Annapurna, and Tukuche Peak are extraordinary.',3660,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(117,30,6,'Day Hike to Khayer Lake','A demanding 840m ascent to the sacred Khayer Lake (4,500m) — a high alpine lake revered by both Hindus and Buddhists. The views from the lake shore are among the finest in the entire Annapurna region. Return to Khopra Danda.',3660,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(118,30,7,'Khopra Danda to Ghandruk','Descend from the ridge through forest to the large Gurung village of Ghandruk — a showcase of traditional Gurung architecture and culture.',1940,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(119,30,8,'Ghandruk to Nayapul, Drive to Pokhara or Kathmandu','Short descent to Nayapul and drive back to Pokhara, then onward to Kathmandu. Tour complete.',820,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(120,31,1,'Drive Kathmandu to Pokhara','Drive or fly to Pokhara. Afternoon preparation for the trek.',820,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(121,31,2,'Drive Pokhara to Beni, Trek to Tatopani','Drive to Beni along the Kali Gandaki and trek upstream to the famous hot spring village of Tatopani.',1190,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(122,31,3,'Tatopani to Chitre','Leave the Kali Gandaki and climb into the Annapurna foothills through apple orchards and terraced farmland.',2390,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(123,31,4,'Chitre to Dagnam','Continue climbing through rhododendron and oak forest. Dagnam is a high settlement with first views of the Dhaulagiri massif.',2800,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(124,31,5,'Dagnam to Khopra Danda','Reach the famous Khopra Danda ridge (3,660m) with extraordinary panoramas. Community lodge accommodation.',3660,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(125,31,6,'Climb to Khayer Lake','The main objective of the trek: ascend 840m to the sacred Khayer Lake (4,500m). Circle the lake on the kora path, soak in the spiritual atmosphere, and take in sweeping views of Dhaulagiri, Annapurna, Nilgiri, and Tukuche. Descend to Khopra Danda.',3660,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(126,31,7,'Khopra Danda to Ghorepani','Traverse east along the ridge through Swanta to Ghorepani, completing a beautiful mountain traverse.',2874,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(127,31,8,'Ghorepani to Nayapul, Drive to Pokhara','Poon Hill optional sunrise, then descend through Ghandruk to Nayapul. Drive to Pokhara.',820,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(128,31,9,'Drive Pokhara to Kathmandu or Departure','Drive back to Kathmandu. Tour ends.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(129,32,1,'Fly Kathmandu to Pokhara','Morning flight to Pokhara. Afternoon at leisure by Phewa Lake. Evening briefing and gear check.',820,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(130,32,2,'Fly Pokhara to Jomsom, Trek to Kagbeni','Mountain flight to Jomsom (2,720m) in the Kali Gandaki valley. Trek upriver to the medieval walled village of Kagbeni — the gateway to the Upper Mustang Restricted Area. Permits checked.',2810,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(131,32,3,'Kagbeni to Chele','Enter the restricted zone and begin trekking into the Mustang plateau. The landscape transforms immediately into dramatic red and ochre canyon badlands. Chele is the first Upper Mustang village.',3050,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(132,32,4,'Chele to Syangboche via Taklam La','Cross the Taklam La (3,624m) and Dajori La passes through some of Mustang\'s most dramatic lunar landscape. Syangboche sits in an open valley with ancient cave settlements visible in the cliff faces.',3800,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(133,32,5,'Syangboche to Ghami','Pass through Ghara and cross the Nyi La (4,010m) with sweeping views of the Tibetan plateau landscape. Ghami has one of Mustang\'s longest mani walls.',3520,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(134,32,6,'Ghami to Tsarang','Visit Ghami Monastery and trek through canyon landscapes to Tsarang — an ancient fortified village with a red dzong (castle) perched on the cliff edge. Extraordinary views.',3620,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(135,32,7,'Tsarang to Lo Manthang','The great day: arrive at Lo Manthang — the medieval walled capital of the Mustang Kingdom. Enter through the single gate into a time capsule of Tibetan culture frozen for centuries. Population of around 1,000 people live inside the ancient walls.',3840,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(136,32,8,'Explore Lo Manthang','Full day to explore the extraordinary contents of the walled city: Jampa Lhakhang, Thubchen, and Chodey gompas with their ancient murals; the King\'s palace; narrow lanes and traditional flat-roofed houses.',3840,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(137,32,9,'Lo Manthang to Drakmar via Namgyal','Visit Namgyal and Lo Gekar — the oldest monastery in Mustang — before descending into the dramatic red-cliffed valley of Drakmar. The ancient cave dwellings here are extraordinary.',3810,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(138,32,10,'Drakmar to Ghami via Charang','Return route via the high plateau, passing sky caves and ancient cliff monasteries. The scale of the landscape is immense.',3520,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(139,32,11,'Ghami to Chuksang via Tangbe','Descend through the villages of Tangbe — famous for its white-walled houses and black-and-white-striped chortens — and Chuksang.',2980,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(140,32,12,'Chuksang to Jomsom via Kagbeni','Return through Kagbeni (exiting the restricted area) and continue along the Kali Gandaki to Jomsom. The valley wind can be ferocious in the afternoon.',2720,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(141,32,13,'Fly Jomsom to Pokhara, Drive to Kathmandu','Morning mountain flight Jomsom–Pokhara. Afternoon drive or fly to Kathmandu.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(142,32,14,'Departure','Transfer to Tribhuvan International Airport. Upper Mustang — the Forbidden Kingdom — has revealed its secrets.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(143,36,1,'Drive Kathmandu to Syabrubesi','7–8 hour scenic drive through forested hills and river valleys to the road-head at Syabrubesi. Overnight at guesthouse.',1503,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(144,36,2,'Syabrubesi to Lama Hotel','The trail enters Langtang National Park immediately. Trek through rhododendron and bamboo forest along the Langtang Khola river canyon, passing Bamboo, Riverside, and Gumnachowk.',2470,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(145,36,3,'Lama Hotel to Langtang Village','Forest gives way to open yak pastures as the valley widens dramatically. Pass Ghoda Tabela (the old army post) and climb to the rebuilt Langtang Village — devastated in the 2015 earthquake and reconstructed by the community.',3430,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(146,36,4,'Langtang Village to Kyanjin Gompa','Trek across open moraine and yak pastures to the beautiful Kyanjin Gompa monastery at the head of the valley. Langtang Lirung (7,227m) rises directly above. Visit the famous yak cheese dairy.',3870,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(147,36,5,'Acclimatization Day at Kyanjin Gompa','Hike up Kyanjin Ri (4,773m) for a 360° panorama of Langtang Lirung, Langtang II, and Dorje Lakpa. Alternatively explore the Langshisha Kharka valley. Visit the ancient Kyanjin Gompa monastery.',3870,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(148,36,6,'Kyanjin Gompa to Lama Hotel','Begin the return descent through Langtang Village and the rhododendron and bamboo forest zones. The descent is rapid and enjoyable.',2470,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(149,36,7,'Lama Hotel to Syabrubesi, Drive toward Kathmandu','Complete the descent to Syabrubesi and begin the long drive back toward Kathmandu.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(150,36,8,'Arrival Kathmandu or Departure','Arrive in Kathmandu or transfer to airport.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(151,37,1,'Drive Kathmandu to Syabrubesi','Drive through forested hills to Syabrubesi, the gateway to Langtang National Park.',1503,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(152,37,2,'Syabrubesi to Lama Hotel','Trek through the lower Langtang gorge through bamboo and rhododendron forest.',2470,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(153,37,3,'Lama Hotel to Langtang Village','Valley opens to wide yak pastures. Trek to the rebuilt Langtang Village.',3430,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(154,37,4,'Langtang Village to Kyanjin Gompa','Trek across open moraine to the monastery at the head of the valley.',3870,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(155,37,5,'Acclimatization Day at Kyanjin Gompa','Day hike up Kyanjin Ri (4,773m) for spectacular Langtang Lirung panorama.',3870,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(156,37,6,'Kyanjin Gompa to Lama Hotel','Rapid descent through the Langtang Valley to Lama Hotel.',2470,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(157,37,7,'Lama Hotel to Thulo Syabru','Branch off the main trail and climb through forest to the large village of Thulo Syabru, perched on a spur with wide valley views.',2212,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(158,37,8,'Thulo Syabru to Sing Gompa','A steady climb through forest past cheese factories and yak pastures to the cluster of lodges at Sing Gompa, beneath a beautiful old monastery.',3330,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(159,37,9,'Sing Gompa to Lauribinayak','Climb through forests and across open ridges to the high camp below Lauribinayak pass. The Himalayan panorama from this ridge is extraordinary.',4610,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(160,37,10,'Cross Lauribinayak Pass (4,610m) to Gosainkunda','The high point of the trek. Cross the Lauribinayak ridge and descend to the sacred Gosainkunda Lake (4,380m) — the spiritual centrepiece of this trek. The lake is revered in both Hindu and Buddhist traditions. Camp or lodge.',4380,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(161,37,11,'Gosainkunda to Ghopte via Lauribinayak','Descend the eastern side of the ridge through high rhododendron and bamboo forest to Ghopte.',3430,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(162,37,12,'Ghopte to Melamchi Pul Bazaar','Long descent through the Melamchi valley back to the valley floor and the road at Melamchi Pul.',823,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(163,37,13,'Drive Melamchi Pul to Kathmandu','Drive back to Kathmandu through the hills. Arrive by late afternoon.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(164,37,14,'Kathmandu Rest and Sightseeing','Free day in Kathmandu for final sightseeing, shopping, or relaxation.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(165,37,15,'Departure','Transfer to Tribhuvan International Airport.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(166,39,1,'Drive Kathmandu to Babare (Sindhupalchowk)','Drive northeast from Kathmandu along the Araniko Highway to Babare, the starting point.',1000,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(167,39,2,'Babare to Mahankal Bhanjyang','Trek through traditional villages and terraced farmland, climbing steadily toward the ridgeline.',1800,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(168,39,3,'Mahankal Bhanjyang to Thotane','Cross the ridge and descend into the Panch Pokhari valley. The forest becomes denser with rhododendron at higher elevations.',2750,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(169,39,4,'Thotane to Panch Pokhari','Final ascent to the five sacred alpine lakes of Panch Pokhari (4,100m). The approach reveals increasingly dramatic mountain views as the tree line recedes.',4100,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(170,39,5,'Explore Panch Pokhari','Explore all five sacred lakes. The largest lake has a small shrine visited by Hindu pilgrims during Janai Purnima festival. Views of the Jugal Himal and distant Everest. Rest and acclimatize.',4100,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(171,39,6,'Return to Thotane','Begin the return descent back through the forest zones.',2750,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(172,39,7,'Thotane to Babare, Drive toward Kathmandu','Complete descent to road-head and drive back.',1000,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(173,39,8,'Arrival Kathmandu or Departure','Arrive in Kathmandu or transfer to airport.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(174,41,1,'Drive Kathmandu to Singati Bazaar (Dolakha)','Drive east toward Dolakha district to the road-head at Singati Bazaar. The drive takes around 5–6 hours.',1150,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(175,41,2,'Singati Bazaar to Gongar','Begin trekking up the Rolwaling valley through subtropical forest and scattered settlements.',1450,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(176,41,3,'Gongar to Simigaon','Trek through rice terraces and forest to the traditional Tamang village of Simigaon with views toward the high mountains ahead.',2005,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(177,41,4,'Simigaon to Dongang','The trail climbs more steeply into the Rolwaling Valley. The landscape becomes increasingly alpine and remote.',2850,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(178,41,5,'Dongang to Beding','Enter the heart of the Rolwaling Valley and reach Beding — a remarkable Tibetan-origin community at the foot of the high peaks. The village has an ancient gompa and warm hospitality.',3693,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(179,41,6,'Acclimatization Day in Beding','Rest and acclimatize. Day hike toward the Drangka Glacier or Rolwaling peaks. Explore Beding\'s monastery and learn about the unique Sherpa-Tibetan culture of this remote valley.',3693,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(180,41,7,'Beding to Na','Trek further up the valley through open yak pastures to the summer herding settlement of Na. The glacial peaks are now very close.',4183,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(181,41,8,'Day Hike to Tsho Rolpa Lake','A challenging day hike to Tsho Rolpa (4,580m), one of Nepal\'s largest glacial lakes. The turquoise water fills a dramatic glacial basin. Return to Na for the night.',4183,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(182,41,9,'Na to Beding','Return through the valley, the altitude descent bringing renewed energy.',3693,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(183,41,10,'Beding to Simigaon','Descend back through the lower valley.',2005,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(184,41,11,'Simigaon to Singati, Drive toward Kathmandu','Complete the descent and begin the drive back.',1150,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(185,41,12,'Arrival Kathmandu or Departure','Arrive Kathmandu or transfer to airport.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(186,43,1,'Fly Kathmandu to Jumla','Scenic mountain flight to Jumla (2,370m) in Nepal\'s far west. One of the most dramatic short flights in Nepal. Afternoon orientation in Jumla town.',2370,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(187,43,2,'Jumla to Khali','Begin the trek through pine and juniper forest, climbing steadily northwest toward Rara National Park.',2830,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(188,43,3,'Khali to Sinja (Sinja Valley)','Trek through the historic Sinja Valley — the ancient capital of the medieval Khas Kingdom where Nepali language originated. Pass ancient ruins and traditional villages.',2450,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(189,43,4,'Sinja to Jaljala','Cross the Jaljala Pass (3,770m) with panoramic views of far-western Nepal\'s peaks. Descend toward the Rara basin.',3770,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(190,43,5,'Jaljala to Rara Lake','Descend through pristine forests to the shores of Rara Lake (2,990m) — Nepal\'s largest lake. The colour of the water changes throughout the day from deep blue to turquoise to silver. Lodge accommodation near the lake shore.',2990,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(191,43,6,'Rest and Explore Rara Lake','Full day to explore the lake and Rara National Park. Trek the kora (circumambulation) around the lake shores through mixed forest. Birdwatching: 214 bird species recorded. Wildlife: red deer, langur monkey, bear.',2990,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(192,43,7,'Rara to Pina','Begin the return via a different route through the national park to the village of Pina.',2423,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(193,43,8,'Pina to Jumla','Complete the return trek to Jumla.',2370,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(194,43,9,'Fly Jumla to Kathmandu','Morning flight back to Kathmandu.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(195,43,10,'Departure','Transfer to Tribhuvan International Airport.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(196,45,1,'Fly Kathmandu to Nepalgunj, Fly to Juphal','Morning flight to Nepalgunj and onward connecting flight to Juphal airstrip (2,475m) in Dolpa district.',2475,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(197,45,2,'Juphal to Dunai','Trek down to the district headquarters of Dunai on the banks of the Bheri River.',2145,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(198,45,3,'Dunai to Tarakot','Trek upstream along the Suli Gad river through a dramatic river gorge.',2540,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(199,45,4,'Tarakot to Chhepka','Enter Shey Phoksundo National Park. The trail climbs through progressively dramatic scenery.',2960,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(200,45,5,'Chhepka to Amchi','Descend to the Suli Gad river and climb back up toward the Phoksundo Lake basin. The trail passes through ancient Bon villages.',3630,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(201,45,6,'Amchi to Phoksundo Lake (Ringmo)','Arrive at the impossibly blue Phoksundo Lake (3,611m) — Nepal\'s deepest lake and one of the world\'s most beautiful. The turquoise water, set against red canyon walls and snow peaks, is unforgettable.',3611,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(202,45,7,'Explore Phoksundo Lake and Monastery','Full day at the lake. Visit the ancient Bon monastery on the cliff above. Walk the lake shores. Marvel at the cascading Phoksundo waterfall at the lake\'s outlet.',3611,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(203,45,8,'Phoksundo to Amchi','Begin the return journey back through the national park.',3630,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(204,45,9,'Amchi to Sulighat','Descend through the gorge toward the lower Dolpo valleys.',2470,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(205,45,10,'Sulighat to Tarakot','Continue the return trek downstream.',2540,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(206,45,11,'Tarakot to Dunai','Return to the district headquarters of Dunai.',2145,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(207,45,12,'Dunai to Juphal, Fly to Nepalgunj','Trek to Juphal and fly to Nepalgunj.',154,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(208,45,13,'Fly Nepalgunj to Kathmandu','Morning flight back to Kathmandu. Afternoon rest.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(209,45,14,'Departure','Transfer to Tribhuvan International Airport.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(210,49,1,'Drive Kathmandu to Besisahar','Drive along the Prithvi Highway to Besisahar, the starting point for the Marsyangdi valley approach.',760,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(211,49,2,'Drive to Koto, Trek to Meta','Drive further up the valley to Koto where Nar Phu restricted area permits are verified. Trek into the dramatic Nar Phu side valley to Meta village.',3560,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(212,49,3,'Meta to Phu Village','Trek up the Phu Khola valley through a narrow gorge to the remarkable Phu Village — a medieval fortress settlement at 4,080m with a commanding position above the valley.',4080,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(213,49,4,'Explore Phu Village','Full day to explore Phu village with its ancient stone houses, Buddhist gompa, and extraordinary views of Himlung Himal and Kang Guru. This village is among the most remote and authentic communities in Nepal.',4080,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(214,49,5,'Phu to Nar Village via Kang La Pass','Cross the formidable Kang La Pass (5,320m) — a demanding but extraordinary high-altitude crossing with views of Manaslu, Annapurna, and the Tibetan plateau. Descend to the equally remote Nar village.',4110,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(215,49,6,'Explore Nar Village','Rest and acclimatize in Nar. Explore the village\'s ancient fortifications, chortens, and monastery. The culture here is almost entirely Tibetan Buddhist despite being within Nepal.',4110,1,NULL,NULL,NULL),(216,49,7,'Nar to Ngawal','Descend from the Nar Phu plateau back into the main Annapurna Circuit valley via the Kangla Phedi trail to Ngawal.',3657,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(217,49,8,'Ngawal to Manang','Walk the high trail along the Annapurna Circuit to Manang — the region\'s main acclimatization hub.',3540,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(218,49,9,'Manang to Yak Kharka','Ascend toward the Thorong La. Yak Kharka is the last settlement with substantial services before the pass.',4018,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(219,49,10,'Yak Kharka to Thorong High Camp','Short climb to the base camp below Thorong La. Rest thoroughly and prepare for the pre-dawn start.',4925,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(220,49,11,'Cross Thorong La Pass (5,416m) to Muktinath','The culminating crossing of the trek. Start before 5am and climb to the top of Thorong La (5,416m) as the sun rises. Descend 1,656m to the sacred Hindu and Buddhist pilgrimage town of Muktinath.',3760,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(221,49,12,'Muktinath to Jomsom, Fly to Pokhara','Drive or trek to Jomsom and take the morning mountain flight to Pokhara.',820,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(222,49,13,'Drive Pokhara to Kathmandu or Departure','Drive back to Kathmandu or take the Pokhara–Kathmandu flight.',1400,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(223,21,1,'Fly to Lukla, Trek to Phakding','Mountain flight Kathmandu–Lukla. First day on the Khumbu trail to Phakding.',2652,0,NULL,NULL,NULL),(224,21,2,'Phakding to Namche Bazaar','Classic second day crossing suspension bridges to the Sherpa capital.',3440,0,NULL,NULL